I saw that as a problem, as I thought people were giving A.I. too much credit on it's good days (which has always been incredible)... and not recognising the ways it misbehaves and falls over (which has received much less press).

The Claude 3.5 Sonnet model from Anthropic has changed my mind. It's not perfect, but it understands some of my computer programs better than I do... and when I say understand, I mean in the very human sense.

Here is an expert-level conversation with this model. I apologise for the technical language... but I wanted to get a taste of it's response. Scroll to the end for the non-technical description.


